Console output from a Play-mode session, Studio, solo client "Demiurgos_18".
Config at capture time: Round.Intermission=8, Round.Duration=20, Round.EndScreen=6,
Debug.SoloTesting=true, Debug.VerboseLogging=true, Debug.ForceAswangWhenSolo=false (unset — committed default).

Five full round cycles (#1-#5) ran back to back. In every one:
  - "[RoleService] Drew 1 roles." fires at the top of INTERMISSION.
  - The client's own snapshot line stays "you: ALIVE" through STARTING, ACTIVE and ENDING every round.
  - No [MonsterService] line of any kind appears anywhere in the log — no transform, no kill, no
    "Refused feed", no "Feed broken". The Aswang-side code path never ran once in 5 rounds.
  - The on-screen HUD role card (screen_capture, viewed but not persisted to disk — no tool in this
    session's toolset writes a Studio screen_capture image to a file path) read "SURVIVOR" during
    round #1's ACTIVE phase.

This matches RoleService.luau's own documented behaviour: `RoleDraw.draw` clamps picks to
`#candidates - 1`, so a 1-candidate pool always keeps that candidate as a survivor — deterministically,
not probabilistically. The only override is `Config.Debug.ForceAswangWhenSolo`, gated to
`RunService:IsStudio() and SoloTesting and ForceAswangWhenSolo and #candidates <= MinPlayers`, which
was left at its committed default of `false` for this run. With one real client and no husk on the
board (husks are created only by a player leaving/idling, not present at round start), there is no way
to reach `beginFeed` — the function this whole chunk (V06) is about — without that flag.

